## Summary

Your test exposed a real gap: my earlier registration only ran when a *new* worktree got provisioned (fresh `SessionStart` or the lazy fallback), never on an already-resolved session — so deleting the main-checkout record while the worktree itself stayed intact would never self-heal.

**Fixed**: added `mirror_worktree_assignment_to_main` in [main.rs](memory-api/crates/session-capture-hook/src/main.rs), called on **every** successful capture (any trigger that reaches persistence, so `Stop` included once a real assignment exists). It reads the worktree's own just-captured `metadata.worktree` and mirrors it into the main checkout's registry via the existing `register_provisioned_worktree`, best-effort and idempotent.

- Added `e2e_user_prompt_submit_self_heals_a_deleted_main_checkout_registration` reproducing exactly your test: `SessionStart` → registers → delete the main-checkout record → `UserPromptSubmit` → record reappears.
- All 31 `session-capture-hook` tests + `session-api` tests pass.
- Reinstalled the binary; confirmed against the log that this session's own record (deleted by your test) reappeared at `2026-08-19T01:20:15Z` from a real organic `PostToolUse` hook, not leftover test state.",
